Plate looks like a square side plate, roughly 22 cm across. The strips (likely tempeh bacon or smoked tofu or seitan strips) cover about 20% of the plate, are thin (about 0.8 cm), and there are about 6 strips, each roughly 12 x 2.5 x 0.8 cm = 24 cm³, so about 140 cm³ in total. That is too high given the overlap and tapering, so I estimate about 80 g.

The spinach salad covers about 18% of the plate, is about 2 cm high, and is loosely packed. I estimate about 45 g of cooked or wilted spinach, plus about 8 g of carrot shreds, with a little dressing.

